WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.840
In Season 1, you saw that we found a small&nbsp;
water reservoir right next to Basekamp.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.028
We cleared around it.

00:00:10.756 --> 00:00:13.187
And, we went in to explore this delicious water.

00:00:15.626 --> 00:00:19.109
But, we got busy with a lot of other&nbsp;stuff 
and somehow forgot about it.

00:00:19.109 --> 00:00:22.670
So, now, two years later,
 we're going to give it a big&nbsp;makeover.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.776
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update.

00:00:27.563 --> 00:00:30.797
Hey! So, here we are next to our lake/pond/
water reservoir...

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.519
I don't know how you call this...

00:00:32.867 --> 00:00:37.724
We cleaned this up in the beginning,
 when we came&nbsp;to this land actually, but left it ever since...

00:00:38.249 --> 00:00:41.892
In the beginning, there was a lot of water,
 but now&nbsp;it's the middle of summer, so it almost dried up.

00:00:42.066 --> 00:00:43.583
But, there's still some water...

00:00:44.542 --> 00:00:47.019
So, currently, it's quite&nbsp;a good time to rework it.

00:00:47.019 --> 00:00:51.077
Because, then we can do it before 
the winter season starts and all the&nbsp;rain gets in.

00:00:51.077 --> 00:00:54.762
And it also becomes more and more useful
 to have this reservoir around...

00:00:54.762 --> 00:00:59.313
Because, as you can&nbsp;see from above,
 here's Basekamp and here's the reservoir.

00:00:59.313 --> 00:01:04.361
It's currently a bit overgrown&nbsp;around mimosas,
 but it's quite useful to have a big chunk of water here.

00:01:04.361 --> 00:01:07.042
In case of a fire, or just&nbsp;to cool down.

00:01:07.042 --> 00:01:10.711
So, before we're going to work on it,
 let me show you what it actually looks like.

00:01:10.711 --> 00:01:18.290
And, I'm&nbsp;going to show you first person, so you can really see 
why we want to rework this thing with a GoPro.

00:01:18.638 --> 00:01:21.422
All right! So, first up:

00:01:21.422 --> 00:01:24.870
This is what it looks like from here...

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:32.686
And, as you can see, a lot&nbsp;of vegetation started to grow back 
around the edges, which could be cleaned up.

00:01:32.686 --> 00:01:38.360
Secondly, as you can see here, it start to really erode.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.700
So, the whole area, the wall is super steep,
 and it&nbsp;was really dug out.

00:01:42.944 --> 00:01:46.205
Which, every now and then it just collapses like here.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.360
So, slowly the whole&nbsp;wall eroded.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:53.947
Also there, the only thing really that keeps it up
 is all the mimosa trees right there.

00:01:54.373 --> 00:01:57.749
The roots maintain a little bit of the structure.

00:01:57.749 --> 00:02:01.784
And, the whole wall is really just like crumbling&nbsp;apart.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:08.123
These roots still give some strength to it.

00:02:11.521 --> 00:02:13.826
It's very delicious water...

00:02:15.916 --> 00:02:18.732
And it's still pretty deep, I think, in&nbsp;the middle.

00:02:20.265 --> 00:02:25.055
And, here in the back, there's still a lot of 
old, dead trees from the fire.

00:02:25.055 --> 00:02:26.546
As you can&nbsp;see, they burned down.

00:02:27.173 --> 00:02:34.920
But, this height difference is really big, 
so here's a big road on top and slowly&nbsp;this erodes more as well.

00:02:35.949 --> 00:02:38.891
So, we want to clean it up.

00:02:53.175 --> 00:02:57.628
The reason why it looks like this&nbsp;is that the 
previous owner saw some water here.

00:02:57.628 --> 00:03:00.944
And, he just dug it out, so there was&nbsp;more water available.

00:03:00.944 --> 00:03:02.673
That's why the walls are so steep.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.144
And, they also say&nbsp;there used to be a pipe from here to the bottom of the land.

00:03:07.144 --> 00:03:10.112
We've never seen it, but the neighbors keep talking about it.

00:03:10.112 --> 00:03:15.316
To distribute the water across the land,
 so maybe we'll find that when working on it.

00:03:17.894 --> 00:03:20.005
It becomes a bit swampy.

00:03:20.005 --> 00:03:22.120
And, the water level, as you can see, is now here.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:27.184
But, originally, it's there like right under where all the root&nbsp;start,
which is more in the winter time.

00:03:27.358 --> 00:03:31.782
So it would be here. So it's quite a big difference that it fills up in the winter.

00:03:31.782 --> 00:03:38.149
And also, Mattia dropped in the first year when we came here,
 and we started cleaning these up, pliers here or scissors.

00:03:39.124 --> 00:03:41.472
- Yeah, my phone just dropped in there.

00:03:42.456 --> 00:03:44.308
No, the scissors just dropped in there...

00:03:45.353 --> 00:03:45.853
- Fuck!

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:48.767
So, maybe we're going to find that back as well,

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:49.540
I hope so!

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:50.555
I'm curious to see what it looks like.

00:03:50.555 --> 00:03:53.541
But, let me show you the coolest part, 
which we can see right&nbsp;here now.

00:03:53.541 --> 00:03:55.748
Because, it's summer and the water level is low.

00:03:57.389 --> 00:03:59.747
But, this used to be a natural spring!

00:04:00.731 --> 00:04:07.018
So, here, it's very moist, because somewhere 
in this area was a natural spring.

00:04:07.937 --> 00:04:10.919
Which makes sure the water just flows here.

00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:15.470
You can see little bits of it!

00:04:18.584 --> 00:04:22.863
So, I'm not sure if you can see it, but here you can see the water coming back.

00:04:23.191 --> 00:04:26.870
Even though the water level is higher than there.

00:04:27.274 --> 00:04:31.290
So, this is where the spring used to be around here.

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:34.921
But, I'm not sure if it's still active, and how much it gives...

00:04:34.921 --> 00:04:38.648
So, the&nbsp;moment we start digging, I guess we're going to see better.

00:04:40.982 --> 00:04:43.758
The plan: we're first going to clean&nbsp;up a little bit around it.

00:04:43.758 --> 00:04:45.424
And, take some dead trees out

00:04:45.424 --> 00:04:47.307
Also, there's a lot of stuff laying around.

00:04:47.899 --> 00:04:54.160
Then, we're going to pump the lagoon empty, 
so we can see how deep it actually is.

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:58.946
To see&nbsp;if we find some other things there, and also...

00:04:58.946 --> 00:05:03.157
To see if the the spring renews itself, 
&nbsp;and what the water table level actually is.

00:05:03.157 --> 00:05:06.761
And then, with a digger,
 we're going to clean up&nbsp;these eroded edges.

00:05:06.761 --> 00:05:10.969
We'll put them under angle,
so it doesn't collapse anymore when the water&nbsp;gets in.

00:05:11.527 --> 00:05:14.967
And then, we also start cleaning up in that area,
 where we find a lot of mimosas.

00:05:14.967 --> 00:05:16.924
We're going to keep the mimosas for the roots.

00:05:16.924 --> 00:05:21.760
But, in between, there's a lot of firewood, 
which is a lot of dead wood, which is a fire hazard...

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:23.729
So, we're going to clean that up as&nbsp;well.

00:05:23.729 --> 00:05:26.539
Hopefully, in the end, there's going to be a nice area here.

00:05:27.096 --> 00:05:28.129
But, let's see!

00:05:28.129 --> 00:05:29.571
I've never done this&nbsp;before.

00:05:29.571 --> 00:05:34.582
We start by pulling out some brambles and spiky bushes.

00:06:11.081 --> 00:06:13.643
So, the front part is now clean&nbsp;enough.

00:06:13.643 --> 00:06:18.108
Now, we need to go to the back, 
but let me bring you closer, so you can see what it looks like.

00:06:18.108 --> 00:06:19.497
Because, it's a bit more rough!

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:22.835
So, the back part here -- we never cleaned it up before...

00:06:22.835 --> 00:06:25.126
So, there's&nbsp;still a lot of old dead trees.

00:06:25.126 --> 00:06:28.980
And it's very steep and eroding,
 so it's going to be a bit harder to clean&nbsp;this up.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.908
But, I guess we're just going to go for it!

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.701
So, it's now all cleaned up.

00:08:06.701 --> 00:08:10.727
As you might have seen,&nbsp;it's pretty steep and everything crumbles down.

00:08:11.416 --> 00:08:14.645
But, there are a few natural things that happen to&nbsp;prevent this.

00:08:14.645 --> 00:08:16.051
Let me show you!

00:08:16.051 --> 00:08:21.593
So, what happens is that every now and then,
 a stick falls sideways, like here or there.

00:08:21.593 --> 00:08:25.352
And, it gets stuck between the&nbsp;trees, so it cannot slide down.

00:08:25.352 --> 00:08:33.353
And then, all&nbsp;the little smaller sticks and branches,
 they're getting stuck between there, which creates a&nbsp;bit of a terrace...

00:08:34.259 --> 00:08:36.250
Also a little bit of a stairs.

00:08:43.269 --> 00:08:47.427
And, this is useful, because it prevents everything sliding down.

00:08:47.427 --> 00:08:49.209
So, you have a bit of a shield.

00:08:49.209 --> 00:08:52.347
It also retains some water, which is good!

00:08:52.741 --> 00:08:59.557
And, in the end, the main thing is just that 
not the whole lake gets full of sticks...

00:09:00.148 --> 00:09:03.252
Now, there actually are little sticks, which I just took out.

00:09:03.252 --> 00:09:07.611
We're going to use the big ones to&nbsp;really build 
more of these enforcements between the trees.

00:09:07.611 --> 00:09:13.096
So, we create a bunch of terraces that&nbsp;we can walk up,
 and to have this whole area a bit stronger.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.817
So, that's going to be the principle.

00:09:34.817 --> 00:09:37.425
Now, we are just going to put more up.

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:35.706
So, next, you need to make some space 
so we&nbsp;have the water here...

00:10:35.706 --> 00:10:39.596
Then, there's some sort of a pathway here and mimosas there.

00:10:39.596 --> 00:10:45.646
But, the&nbsp;digger needs to come in order to make
 this wall less steep, so we need more space here.

00:10:45.646 --> 00:10:48.306
So,&nbsp;we're going to chop some of the mimosa trees.

00:10:48.306 --> 00:10:53.250
The trees are right there and we're going&nbsp;
to use a chainsaw, because it's quite a lot of them.

00:11:55.883 --> 00:11:57.618
So, everything is now chopped!

00:11:57.618 --> 00:11:59.984
Now comes&nbsp;the fun part: moving it...

00:11:59.984 --> 00:12:02.679
We got Jaime helping out for that.

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:58.202
All right, so, it's cleaned up here.

00:12:58.596 --> 00:13:00.503
All the&nbsp;the trees are chopped here.

00:13:00.503 --> 00:13:07.319
Now, next, we need to empty this water leftover that is in there&nbsp;
to see what's actually down.

00:13:07.319 --> 00:13:11.800
To see how deep it is, and maybe we find that plier,
 or the pipe that&nbsp;the neighbors say is there...

00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:14.804
Or, maybe we even find a suitcase of gold!

00:13:14.804 --> 00:13:16.132
It could easily be the case.

00:13:16.132 --> 00:13:18.009
Let's see, and pump it up!

00:13:18.009 --> 00:13:20.230
So, here we have a water pump.

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:23.149
It has two hoses -- one where the&nbsp;water goes in, and one out.

00:13:23.149 --> 00:13:26.498
The downside is the incoming hose is not super long...

00:13:28.204 --> 00:13:29.773
That's&nbsp;just the one we had.

00:13:30.587 --> 00:13:39.081
And, I made a filter from an old little jerrican with some holes
 to&nbsp;make sure all the dirt and stuff doesn't go in the pump...

00:13:39.639 --> 00:13:44.340
So, ideally now, we just put it in&nbsp;there 
and let it run till it's empty.

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.243
Let's see!

00:14:21.538 --> 00:14:24.135
As we were pumping the water, we ran into&nbsp;some problems...

00:14:24.135 --> 00:14:25.920
The engine of the pump stopped all the time.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:29.187
And, if it was running, it actually didn't&nbsp;really suck anymore.

00:14:29.646 --> 00:14:32.529
We tried a bunch of things, but we're not sure what's going on.

00:14:32.529 --> 00:14:34.894
We're still new to the&nbsp;world of water pumps.

00:14:34.894 --> 00:14:37.252
So, we asked an old expert for help...

00:14:45.567 --> 00:14:49.686
Our neighbor Antonio, and his&nbsp;50-year-old water pump.

00:14:49.686 --> 00:14:51.430
Look at that beast!

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:53.420
And, he has his own filter system.

00:14:53.420 --> 00:14:55.490
An improvisation guy just like us.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:15:03.462
So, to get going, we connected the tube on the bottom,
 then the top, do a little magical thing with the engine...

00:15:05.167 --> 00:15:07.052
Wind up the old rope.

00:15:09.839 --> 00:15:13.943
Get some grip on that kitchen knife 
and do one good pull!

00:15:16.799 --> 00:15:17.800
Very smooth.

00:15:18.323 --> 00:15:20.985
So, water is&nbsp;coming out, but it could be more!

00:15:20.985 --> 00:15:22.548
So, we need to do some wiggling.

00:15:26.875 --> 00:15:28.883
And, meanwhile, the pump is going strong.

00:15:28.883 --> 00:15:33.487
Yeah sure, some leaks, but the lid is popping 
and the knife is dancing.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:35.804
And, the water is flowing.

00:15:35.804 --> 00:15:38.293
So, now, we just have to wait for the water to go.

00:16:01.251 --> 00:16:03.737
The last part was pretty hard to&nbsp;empty up.

00:16:03.737 --> 00:16:07.187
While reaching the bottom, 
it got very muddy and stuff started to appear...

00:16:07.909 --> 00:16:09.833
I see something there!

00:16:19.807 --> 00:16:21.322
And, it also got very smelly...

00:16:21.322 --> 00:16:24.934
Look&nbsp;at all the gas bubbles around my feet 
popping up when walking around!

00:16:26.746 --> 00:16:28.928
Ok, but&nbsp;now, it's empty enough for the next step:

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:31.614
The digger.

00:16:51.777 --> 00:16:54.854
The first step for the digger&nbsp;is to take out
 all the dirt that is in there.

00:16:54.854 --> 00:16:59.268
Some of it is trash, but mostly it's&nbsp;fallen sticks, 
burned trees and some some leaves.

00:18:03.782 --> 00:18:06.454
While digging, we&nbsp;saw a lot of frogs jumping away.

00:18:06.454 --> 00:18:08.002
Especially in the front part.

00:18:08.002 --> 00:18:10.294
So, the frog team jumped in to rescue.

00:18:17.844 --> 00:18:19.681
- It's going to jump out!

00:18:20.865 --> 00:18:23.924
We don't really know if it's an experiment,
 but we saw all these frogs!

00:18:23.924 --> 00:18:30.119
They&nbsp;were going with near the tractor, and we thought:
''Okay, let's try to get some&nbsp;to recreate the biodiversity.'' 

00:18:30.677 --> 00:18:33.169
In the bucket, we have many, many things to be accounted for.

00:18:41.897 --> 00:18:44.223
We have like 10 of these!

00:18:44.223 --> 00:18:46.152
- Where's the frogs?

00:18:46.546 --> 00:18:50.331
We have frogs, but they are a bit shy.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:52.895
- Let's see...

00:19:07.442 --> 00:19:09.286
So, that&nbsp;was basically a day of digging.

00:19:09.286 --> 00:19:11.062
Most of the dirt is out!

00:19:11.062 --> 00:19:14.270
Especially the last shallow part had a&nbsp;lot of laying around.

00:19:14.664 --> 00:19:19.060
The solid and organic stuff that came out 
was put here on the side.

00:19:19.388 --> 00:19:22.668
It was surprisingly grey compared to the rest of the soil around.

00:19:23.127 --> 00:19:24.724
Well, let me show you what&nbsp;it looks like!

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:26.842
So, the lake is now dug out.

00:19:26.842 --> 00:19:32.020
All the dirt is out, and it's quite a lot deeper&nbsp;than we thought!

00:19:32.615 --> 00:19:34.454
Yeah, which is cool!

00:19:34.454 --> 00:19:37.294
It can hold a lot of water and we also found a few&nbsp;things.

00:19:38.304 --> 00:19:41.675
So, I think we found the pipe that 
the neighbors always talk about.

00:19:41.675 --> 00:19:45.591
It goes to&nbsp;the big ruin, the Community Center,
 on the bottom of the land.

00:19:45.591 --> 00:19:49.261
There used to be this&nbsp;pipe, 
so the water from here can be used there.

00:19:49.261 --> 00:19:52.329
We think it's this pipe, but we're not really&nbsp;sure...

00:19:52.329 --> 00:19:55.306
Because, we also found another pipe, which is a bit smaller.

00:19:55.794 --> 00:19:57.704
A slightly different position.

00:19:57.704 --> 00:20:00.043
We're not&nbsp;sure of what water goes in or out....

00:20:00.461 --> 00:20:02.301
it's kind of a mystery.

00:20:02.301 --> 00:20:04.164
I don't know how you would ever&nbsp;find out where these pipes go...

00:20:04.164 --> 00:20:07.343
So, if you have any suggestions, let us know!

00:20:08.459 --> 00:20:13.250
And, it's now also&nbsp;pretty clear to see 
where the spring is, or where the water is flowing.

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:14.556
Because, its now all empty.

00:20:14.556 --> 00:20:17.154
Here, you see a little bit of water sipping through.

00:20:21.787 --> 00:20:23.798
And, it's really the highest point.

00:20:23.798 --> 00:20:27.627
You can see all the water going down here.

00:20:28.666 --> 00:20:30.899
now it's accumulating there at the&nbsp;
back.

00:20:30.899 --> 00:20:34.292
And, he actually dug a nice hole,
so now we can put the water pump there.

00:20:34.292 --> 00:20:36.366
Because, currently, we're having a break.

00:20:36.366 --> 00:20:37.820
The guy is having some lunch.

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:41.901
So, we can put the pump there to make&nbsp;sure
 it doesn't fill up too much when he comes back...

00:20:41.901 --> 00:20:46.276
And, we're going to work on the edges
 to&nbsp;make sure they're less steep.

00:20:47.063 --> 00:20:52.697
The scissors fell somewhere here,
 but I don't think we're&nbsp;going to find it...

00:20:52.697 --> 00:20:54.915
And, if we're going to find it, it's now on the top.

00:20:54.915 --> 00:20:59.053
So, maybe later, when we'll just 
walk around on the land we would find it.

00:21:04.348 --> 00:21:06.077
- Clean shoes, eh Dave?

00:21:10.571 --> 00:21:13.391
Yeah, it looks a bit like a battlefield&nbsp;at this point.

00:21:13.391 --> 00:21:16.171
And, from above, it actually looks like a big cow poop.

00:21:16.972 --> 00:21:21.544
Next,&nbsp;it was time to reduce the steepness
 on the sides to reduce the inclination.

00:21:21.792 --> 00:21:24.793
And,  this was quite satisfying to watch.

00:22:21.360 --> 00:22:27.173
Next, the guy with the digger still came back 
to do some fine tuning work&nbsp;with a smaller digger.

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:35.149
We didn't film much of this, 
because it didn't&nbsp;seem very interesting.

00:22:35.477 --> 00:22:37.454
Until, he found this...

00:22:44.835 --> 00:22:47.175
It was the scissors Mattia dropped in the water!

00:22:47.872 --> 00:22:49.955
So, after what...?

00:22:49.955 --> 00:22:51.137
2 years in here?

00:22:51.137 --> 00:22:56.541
We found it back when he was digging he found our old wrench.

00:22:56.836 --> 00:22:58.070
Wrench?&nbsp;Clippers?

00:22:58.070 --> 00:22:59.060
I don't know what you call this.

00:22:59.060 --> 00:23:00.649
It's a bit rusty...

00:23:04.272 --> 00:23:07.801
I got pretty curious of the&nbsp;condition of it now,
 and see if it still works.

00:23:10.449 --> 00:23:15.154
So, here we are at the workspace,
trying&nbsp;to see if we can fix this one up.

00:23:15.154 --> 00:23:19.128
All the parts are replaceable, so it should be possible.

00:23:19.128 --> 00:23:20.702
And, some parts are still in good condition!

00:23:21.391 --> 00:23:24.170
But, let's see if we can clean it up.

00:23:25.397 --> 00:23:28.954
So, the&nbsp;aluminum handle with the rubber is still very good!

00:23:28.954 --> 00:23:32.721
Only the real metal parts here&nbsp;are rusty.

00:23:32.721 --> 00:23:36.630
I'm not sure if we can just clean 
the rust away and it would still work...

00:23:37.122 --> 00:23:39.869
And, possibly -- this is the blade that cuts...

00:23:40.164 --> 00:23:42.926
I'm not sure if we can still manage to sharpen that one.

00:23:42.926 --> 00:23:45.259
And, the spring here is missing as well...

00:24:25.880 --> 00:24:32.160
So, here's the blade, but it's still&nbsp;a little bit rough and dull...

00:24:32.160 --> 00:24:35.601
I found a replacement kit which has a blade&nbsp;
and this thing.

00:24:35.601 --> 00:24:37.611
This thing, we need it anyway.

00:24:37.611 --> 00:24:42.030
But, for the blade, I guess I'm trying to going&nbsp;
to see if I can actually sharpen this one.

00:24:42.030 --> 00:24:43.787
Before we're going to need a new one...

00:24:43.787 --> 00:24:46.158
So,&nbsp;then we can keep this for another point in time.

00:24:46.880 --> 00:24:50.266
And, for that, we just going&nbsp;to give it a try with a sharpening stone.

00:24:57.699 --> 00:25:01.164
All right, so, the blade is cleaned up and sharpened again on the edge.

00:25:01.164 --> 00:25:04.216
So, now,&nbsp;it's time for the fun part, which is assembling.

00:25:17.384 --> 00:25:18.398
So, here we are!

00:25:18.825 --> 00:25:23.272
It seems&nbsp;to work good, but let's give it a test.

00:25:44.320 --> 00:25:45.341
So, that was pretty cool.

00:25:45.341 --> 00:25:47.795
I did not expect it would&nbsp;still work that well!

00:25:48.254 --> 00:25:51.529
So, now, the team can use it for their
 next cleaning job to cut bushes.

00:25:51.529 --> 00:25:53.516
Which&nbsp;is actually right now!

00:25:54.125 --> 00:25:58.422
- So, as you can see Dave and the digger
 already did their job here on this&nbsp;side.

00:25:58.422 --> 00:26:02.415
Now, it's time for General Help team to work on that side.

00:26:02.415 --> 00:26:07.093
It's a mess, full of very dry, dead and thin&nbsp;mimosas.

00:26:07.093 --> 00:26:09.784
So, we're mainly going to remove the thinner ones.

00:26:09.784 --> 00:26:13.743
The thick ones are the ones we leave&nbsp;to give some shade
 and also to hold the soil a bit.

00:26:17.645 --> 00:26:21.357
Also, we have to avoid this from
happening while we're working here.

00:26:22.019 --> 00:26:26.915
One of the priorities is to make sure&nbsp;that 
all of the debris doesn't go back into the pond...

00:26:27.821 --> 00:26:29.858
- And, that we also don't go&nbsp;into the pond...

00:26:29.858 --> 00:26:31.174
We also don't go into the pond.

00:27:06.394 --> 00:27:10.194
Barbed wire, our lovely friend,&nbsp;got stuck on the chainsaw.

00:27:10.194 --> 00:27:16.160
Hopefully, nothing major, but it's pretty annoying...

00:27:16.822 --> 00:27:21.096
It's&nbsp;annoying for the people, and annoying for the machines.

00:27:24.092 --> 00:27:25.323
- Nice!

00:27:25.323 --> 00:27:28.350
Okay, one less...

00:28:02.033 --> 00:28:05.650
Now, this whole area has a cleared path.

00:28:05.650 --> 00:28:07.890
So, we have easier access to the pond.

00:28:07.890 --> 00:28:11.015
Not only does it look much nicer, and easier to&nbsp;work around...

00:28:11.015 --> 00:28:14.573
It also prevents most of the soil for going into the water.

00:28:14.573 --> 00:28:17.534
You can see that this looks way&nbsp;better.

00:28:17.534 --> 00:28:18.991
Much more light!

00:28:19.516 --> 00:28:22.424
We have a lovely path to access the whole area.

00:28:22.785 --> 00:28:26.020
All of this stuff that&nbsp;we cut down is now on the floor.

00:28:26.020 --> 00:28:28.556
It looks a bit messy but it's the best for the soil.

00:28:28.556 --> 00:28:29.789
Classic&nbsp;General help stuff!

00:28:29.789 --> 00:28:33.990
Now, it's time for Dave to keep the the rest of the project.

00:28:35.244 --> 00:28:36.714
- Good luck Dave!

00:28:36.714 --> 00:28:39.692
So, next, I'm going to dig an overflow.

00:28:39.692 --> 00:28:42.193
So, if the winter the water level goes up.

00:28:42.193 --> 00:28:47.771
To make&nbsp;sure it doesn't go over all the edges,
 but it has a specific place where it can flow&nbsp;out.

00:28:47.771 --> 00:28:49.584
So, I'm going to dig it right there!

00:28:49.584 --> 00:28:53.185
I'm just going to dig a gutter, just so  that it can go&nbsp;out.

00:28:53.185 --> 00:28:56.390
I'm not going to put in a pipe yet and cover it back up.

00:28:56.390 --> 00:29:00.001
Because, I'm not sure yet what&nbsp;will be 
the appropriate height to put it in.

00:29:00.001 --> 00:29:07.654
So, I'm just going to dig it for now 
and then&nbsp;observe this winter to see how this whole thing behaves.

00:29:12.601 --> 00:29:13.792
I can see what you're thinking!

00:29:13.792 --> 00:29:16.379
That could&nbsp;have been done with a digger, a bit faster.

00:29:16.970 --> 00:29:18.435
I agree...

00:29:33.680 --> 00:29:35.479
Alright, so, the overflow ready!

00:29:35.479 --> 00:29:40.069
Now, we're&nbsp;waiting for rain to come in the winter,
and see how it's going to behave.

00:29:40.069 --> 00:29:43.669
I'm kind of&nbsp;curious how high the water level would get!

00:29:45.655 --> 00:29:50.927
And finally, we leveled the soil&nbsp;a bit more 
and added a seed mix that would provide a ground cover.

00:29:50.927 --> 00:29:55.322
To make sure&nbsp;it doesn't really erode
 and everything sticks together better.

00:29:55.322 --> 00:29:59.726
Which should be&nbsp;happening, when it all starts growing later on.

00:30:27.740 --> 00:30:30.599
All right, so, it's ready! Let me show you the&nbsp;end!

00:30:30.599 --> 00:30:32.975
So, here we have the lake/swamp/lagoon?

00:30:32.975 --> 00:30:35.240
Let me know how I should call this!

00:30:35.240 --> 00:30:38.086
But, we cleared&nbsp;it up and now it's much deeper.

00:30:38.086 --> 00:30:40.219
We can hold much more water, which is cool!

00:30:42.334 --> 00:30:43.720
So, there's already some&nbsp;water in here.

00:30:43.720 --> 00:30:45.436
Some frogs are coming back, which is cool!

00:30:45.436 --> 00:30:50.495
But, the main bulk amount of water
&nbsp;would come in winter, when it would start to rain.

00:30:50.495 --> 00:30:52.979
And, hopefully, to fill up this thing.

00:30:52.979 --> 00:30:56.255
So, here,&nbsp;we have the overflow, and the water level is there.

00:30:56.255 --> 00:30:58.639
We still need to fill up all the&nbsp;way here.

00:30:58.639 --> 00:31:01.827
And, when the water level reaches this point, it flows out there.

00:31:01.827 --> 00:31:04.075
To make sure it doesn't break&nbsp;all the other walls.

00:31:04.584 --> 00:31:08.145
So, at the moment the soil is still very crumbly,

00:31:08.637 --> 00:31:14.247
We added this layer&nbsp;on top with a seed mix 
to provide a ground cover.

00:31:14.247 --> 00:31:19.049
To protect the soil, but also hopefully compact it
 and compress it a bit together.

00:31:19.049 --> 00:31:21.042
Just so it all stays in shape properly.

00:31:21.698 --> 00:31:24.772
We cleaned up this side, so, 
now we can access it properly.

00:31:24.772 --> 00:31:27.573
But, this whole wall is still the same as before...

00:31:27.573 --> 00:31:29.611
We're not sure&nbsp;what we're going to do with it yet.

00:31:29.611 --> 00:31:34.432
And, the plan is first to just see how 
this all behaves, what we&nbsp;just did now.

00:31:34.432 --> 00:31:39.430
And, in the winter after it fills up,
and maybe next year in the summer when it's dry&nbsp;again...

00:31:39.430 --> 00:31:42.011
We can see if we want to rework this wall.

00:31:42.011 --> 00:31:47.357
But, for now, at least we can access it properly,
and observe how it behaves.

00:31:48.089 --> 00:31:49.325
So, that was it for now!

00:31:49.325 --> 00:31:51.904
A pretty big difference before and after!

00:31:52.265 --> 00:31:57.486
It still looks a bit bare and raw, but it will get better as 
the top cover grows and new trees&nbsp;are planted.

00:31:58.273 --> 00:32:02.424
The main upside is that we now have 
a bigger water reservoir close to Basekamp.

00:32:02.424 --> 00:32:04.834
Which will be good in the dry summer months.

00:32:05.252 --> 00:32:08.002
So, we will continue to observe and work on this&nbsp;place.

00:32:08.281 --> 00:32:12.320
It will be nice when the first rain comes,
 to see how this whole evolves.

00:32:12.320 --> 00:32:19.124
And, we will&nbsp;make sure to post some pictures
 on Patreon in the winter on how the process is evolving.

00:32:19.124 --> 00:32:22.119
So,&nbsp;if you want to see that make sure 
to support us, so you can see them!

00:32:22.119 --> 00:32:26.124
Or not, and then you just see&nbsp;it in a video update at some point.

00:32:26.960 --> 00:32:28.125
Anyway, that was it!

00:32:28.125 --> 00:32:30.491
Thank you for watching and see you next&nbsp;time!

00:32:32.375 --> 00:32:35.609
In the next update, we will work on another water area on the land.

00:32:35.609 --> 00:32:37.417
We'll be doing some maintenance around the waterfall.

00:32:37.696 --> 00:32:40.672
And, we will also continue building our house from the pig trailer.

00:32:40.672 --> 00:32:42.605
Thanks&nbsp;for watching, and see you in the next update!

